   "html_text": "The code of rules that rule-consequentialism favours a code comprised of rules that are not too numerous, too complicated, or too demanding can sometimes lead people to do acts that do not have the greatest expected value. For example, following the simpler rule “Don’t steal” will sometimes produce less good consequences than following a more complicated rule “Don’t steal except when … or … or … or … or …”. Another example might be following a rule that allows people to give some degree of prior",
